# GTAgentClinic: example environment (see SECURITY.md).
#
# Scripted NPCs need no key. Set only the variables for your chosen connection.
# Keys belong in the SERVER environment. Never use VITE_ variables or client code.
# Copy this file to .env (git-ignored), replace placeholders, and start with:
# node --env-file=.env bin/agentclinic.mjs
# Nothing loads .env automatically. The game requires Node.js 22.12 or newer.

# ── NPC connections ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Choose a default under AI dialogue → Change… in the title screen.
# Menu settings last until the server restarts. Flags override environment settings,
# which override agentclinic.local.json. auto prefers an Anthropic key, then an
# explicitly enabled Claude Code login, then scripts (see docs/LLM_SOURCES.md).
# AGENTCLINIC_LLM=auto                # auto | api | claude-code | codex | vllm | offline

# Anthropic API
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY
# AGENTCLINIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# OpenAI API: choose OpenAI API in the menu; this key does not enable Codex login.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY

# Custom OpenAI-compatible server: local or remote; key is optional.
# LOCAL_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
# LOCAL_API_MODEL=my-model
# LOCAL_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY

# Codex: run npx codex login in the game folder after package installation.
# AGENTCLINIC_CODEX_NPC_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
# AGENTCLINIC_CODEX_DOCTOR_MODEL=gpt-6-luna

# ── Network (see SECURITY.md → "Who may talk to the server") ────────────────
# PORT=5317
# HOST=127.0.0.1                      # 0.0.0.0 = LAN play: anyone on your network can play on your login
# AGENTCLINIC_ALLOWED_HOSTS=          # extra host names, e.g. mymac.local (same as --allow-host)
# AGENTCLINIC_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=        # other pages allowed to call the API, e.g. http://localhost:3000 (same as --allow-origin)

# ── AI-doctor agents (agents/*.ts) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# AGENTCLINIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5317
